; ted-outmem-memstack-zero (#370): outmem continues with the stack of
; the main loop's dispatch, memstack, which is 0 before the first
; dispatch.  TED alone under inject (alerts answered), the start file has
; one line of 36 characters (46 bytes per line item); its AllocMem fails.
; Correct (the fix of the issue): the alert "Not enough memory for
; operation!", then TED ends with the return code of a failed start, -1
; (#357), and frees what it allocated (track: only the 2 allocations
; every failed start leaves; the empty text outmem leaves when the first
; line fails, #1009, is freed too); the original continues with a7 = 0
; and crashes.
; @fixed #370
; @file bo.bas "abcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyz0123456789\n"
; @source F bo.bas
; @command TEDAB:tools/inject alerts track allocfail=46-46/1 blitz2:ted @FILE@
; @expect stdout "inject: allocfail: 1 allocations failed"
; @expect stdout "inject: alert: Not enough memory for operation!"
; @expect stdout "inject: rc=-1"
; @expect stdout "inject: track: 2 allocations left, 302 bytes"
timeout 20
wait exit
